2. PROJECT OVERVIEW & VALUE PROPOSITION (Descrierea Proiectului)
•	Executive Summary: MAR-ROV is a disruptive technological ecosystem designed to solve the global crisis of hazardous, chemical, and industrial waste management. The project integrates an autonomous fleet of Remotely Operated Vehicles (ROVs) and Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs) with advanced AI and haptic capabilities to harvest, seal, and store hazardous waste materials. Storage is executed inside high-pressure, smart, non-corrosive containers placed strategically in ultra-stable, deep-sea geological zones (abyssal plains).
•	Underlying Asset for Tokenization: Intellectual Property (IP) Rights, international patents (pending/in development), and future software licensing matrix for the autonomous robotic fleet and IoT-enabled smart container network.
•	Target Market Size: The global hazardous waste management market, valued at over $140 Billion, driven by the immediate decommissioning needs of older industrial sites and AI data center energy footprints.
3. TOKENOMICS & FINANCIAL ARCHITECTURE (Structura Financiară a Tokenului)
•	Proposed Token Ticker: $OCEAN
•	Token Type: Regulated Security Token (Asset-Backed Token / RWA).
•	Total Supply: 100,000,000 $OCEAN Tokens (Fixed Supply, Non-Inflationary).
•	Target Fundraising Goal: $5,500,000 USD (Hard Cap) / $1,500,000 USD (Soft Cap).
•	Token Value & Utility Matrix:
1.	Royalty Distribution: Token holders receive a direct pro-rata percentage (e.g., 12%) from global licensing fees paid by governments and private corporations utilizing the MAR-ROV encapsulation technology.
2.	Buyback & Burn Mechanism: 5% of all operational profits generated by marine deployment operations will be used to buy back and burn $OCEAN tokens from the open market, increasing scarcity.
3.	Governance Rights: Sovereign funds or institutional investors holding more than 5% of the total supply gain strategic voting rights regarding geographical deployment zones.
4. REGULATORY compliance & LEGAL FRAMEWORK (Conformitate Legală)
•	Compliance Standard: ERC-3643 (T-REX Protocol) or ERC-1404 (Restricted Token Standard) to ensure fully automated KYC/AML (Know Your Customer / Anti-Money Laundering) checks at the smart-contract level.
•	Target Investor Base: Accredited Investors, Venture Capital (VC) Funds, Institutional Investors, and Sovereign Wealth Funds (Excluding non-accredited retail investors to comply with SEC and ESMA regulations).
•	Intellectual Property Protection: All technological blueprints, AI routing algorithms, and structural designs are legally bound to the issuing Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV), ensuring token holders have direct fractional recourse over the assets.
5. TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS FROM THE TOKENIZATION PLATFORM (Solicitări Tehnice)
The applicant requires the following infrastructure capabilities from the Tokenization Platform:
•	Multi-jurisdictional compliance onboarding (KYC/AML automation).
•	Primary issuance smart-contract deployment with integrated transfer restrictions.
•	Cap table management dashboard and automated quarterly stablecoin (USDT/USDC) dividend distribution tool.
•	Whitelisting mechanisms for verified institutional wallets.
